    "project_template_level_name": "template_building-data-driven-systems-lesson5-level1_choicea_2026",
    "teacher_markdown": "### **Teacher Tips**\r\n\r\n**Students may focus on the animal instead of the information provided**\r\n\r\nSome students will choose an animal based on personal preference rather than examining the data available. Encourage them to compare the records by asking: **\"What information helped you make that choice?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant property:\r\n```javascript\r\nbio\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students recognize how the amount of information can influence decisions.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may assume missing information means something negative**\r\n\r\nStudents may interpret a short or missing bio as evidence that an animal is less friendly, less healthy, or less desirable. Encourage them to distinguish between missing data and actual characteristics by asking: **\"Do we know less about this animal, or is the animal actually different?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant property:\r\n```javascript\r\nbio\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis reinforces that missing information is not the same as negative information.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may overlook how uneven descriptions affect choices**\r\n\r\nAnimals with longer, more detailed bios often seem more appealing because users know more about them. Ask: **\"Would you make the same choice if every animal had the same amount of information?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant comparison:\r\n```javascript\r\nDetailed bio vs. short bio\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis can lead to discussions about how data quality and completeness influence decision-making.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may not recognize data completeness as a fairness issue**\r\n\r\nSome students may notice differences in bio length but not consider the impact. Encourage them to think about representation by asking: **\"If one animal has a detailed description and another has only a few words, does each animal have the same chance of being chosen?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant property:\r\n```javascript\r\nbio\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students connect data completeness to fairness and potential bias in real-world datasets."
  },
